From 660a053aa7e5f920e84c6a8c9ffacb6706fdf0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:37:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Prewarm one shader at a time: the burst froze the page on
 a real GPU

The next world's shaders were all issued at once during the opening transition; the card
compiles them one after another and the pixel transition, which reads the picture back every
frame, waited for all of them (page unresponsive). Now one object per kind of shader, the next
only once the card has finished the last (or a third of a second later without the parallel
compile extension), never during a transition, a chapter turn or the preloader; no compileAsync.
Adaptive density no longer measures during the pixel transitions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Yfam9H7FbQFsBx6yJZ8yW
